  "correct": "D",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Use one trigonometric variable",
      "body": "<p>Use  <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>. Then put <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math> to make the equation quadratic.</p>",
      "recap": "The identity links sine squared and cosine squared at the same angle.",
      "pitfall": "Do not replace <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>.",
      "pause": "Rewrite the equation entirely in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow></math>.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l16",
          "reminder": "The identity links sine squared and cosine squared at the same angle."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Keep only allowed cosine values",
      "body": "<p>The equation becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. Factor it and then apply <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "An algebraic root is useful only if the substituted trigonometric quantity can attain it.",
      "pitfall": "A real root of the quadratic need not be a possible cosine value.",
      "pause": "Which root survives the cosine range?",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l16",
          "reminder": "An algebraic root is useful only if the substituted trigonometric quantity can attain it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Count the stated endpoints",
      "body": "<p>For the surviving value, mark a cosine graph on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math>. One complete period is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "Count solutions throughout the original interval, including closed endpoints.",
      "pitfall": "An endpoint at the end of one period is a distinct angle, but do not count it twice.",
      "pause": "List the angles instead of estimating from a sketch.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l16",
          "reminder": "Count solutions throughout the original interval, including closed endpoints."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>The value <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> is impossible. The solutions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> in the closed interval are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math>.</p><p>There are <strong>3 solutions: D.</strong></p>",
